# T-977: Match on unit constructor using qualified dot-access patterns.
# Color.Green: in match arm position → Pattern::Constructor { tag: "Color.Green", binding: None }.
# Scrutinee Green has Variant tag "Color.Green" — tag equality holds, arm matches.
# The evaluator's match_pattern checks tag != variant_tag, so "Color.Green" == "Color.Green" → match.
#
# Note: the "non-exhaustive match: missing coverage for Green" warning below is expected to
# disappear when T-1003 lands (which populates TyConDef.constructors, allowing coverage
# analysis to recognize qualified patterns as covering constructors).
[
  Color: [type Red Green Blue]
  result: [match Green
    Color.Red:   "red"
    Color.Green: "green"
    Color.Blue:  "blue"]
]
=== out
Dict({"Red": Variant(Color.Red, Null), "Green": Variant(Color.Green, Null), "Blue": Variant(Color.Blue, Null), "result": String("green")})

=== warn
non-exhaustive match: missing coverage for Green at 10:11-13:25
